+# Automatic relative-winding chains (autowind) as fitter input
+
+`autowind` (Vesuvius Challenge community tool) turns a binary surface-mask OME-Zarr and an `umbilicus.json` into
+`relative_windings.json`: one point collection per radial chain of sheet crossings, with cumulative `wind_a`
+(0, 1, 2, ... outward). The fitter at this commit already consumes this format. **No code change is needed.** This
+note and `check_relative_windings.py` explain how to load the file and which config keys matter.
+
+## Loading
+
+The file is a standard `vc_pointcollections_json_version: "1"` document. The fitter picks it up in either of two ways:
+
+* **Conventional path:** put the file at `<dataset>/relative_windings.json`. `fit_session.PCL_ROLE_CONVENTIONS` maps
+  that name to `PclRole.RELATIVE`.
+* **Explicit path:** list it under `paths.pcls` with `"role": "relative"`.
+
+Any file name other than `abs_winding.json` is read as relative (`winding_is_absolute = False`). Every point carries
+`wind_a`, so `normalise_pcl_winding_annotations` keeps all of them.
+
+Points that are not attached to a verified patch become **unattached strips** (`get_unattached_pcl_strip_losses`).
+With `input_disable_patches = true`, which is how the chains were validated, every point is unattached.
+
+## Required overrides
+
+```sh
+FIT_SPIRAL_CONFIG_OVERRIDES='{"pcl_unattached_pcl_min_point_spacing": 0.0,
+                              "loss_weight_unattached_pcl_radius": 10.0, ...}' \
+python fit_spiral.py --dataset <dataset>
+```
+
+* `pcl_unattached_pcl_min_point_spacing = 0`. The default of 16 vox greedily drops strip points closer than 16 vox.
+  Chain points are consecutive sheet crossings, about one sheet pitch apart (~16 vox on PHerc0139, ~26 vox on
+  PHerc1667 at ~9.5 um). The default would drop 22 % and 13.7 % of the points, and with them winding steps.
+* `loss_weight_unattached_pcl_radius = 10` (default 2). This weight was validated on PHerc0139 and PHerc1667.
+  A wrong step shifts every later point of its chain by one turn, so the weight trades chain errors against the
+  other losses. Only global weights exist; per-step confidences in the chain file are not used.
+
+The coordinates are `p = [x, y, z]` in the voxel frame of the mask, which must be the fit frame. Pass the fitter the
+same umbilicus that autowind used: autowind writes it as `umbilicus_maskframe.json`.
+
+## Check before fitting
+
+```sh
+python check_relative_windings.py <dataset>/relative_windings.json [--umbilicus <dataset>/umbilicus.json]
+```
+
+The script parses the file with this commit's `point_collection` loader and checks that `wind_a` never decreases
+within a chain. It also reports how many points the default 16-vox spacing would drop. With `--umbilicus`, it adds
+the largest angular jump between consecutive points (a chain is one radial ray, so this should be near 0).
